# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4-seats8-262k window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/seats8-262k and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN.
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. Every value is final.
# ORDER.txt says the order, each job's stop rule, its minutes and the GO rule. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-262k8-1 is the STAGE-2 image: built by SB9 from the commit
# that records the stage-1 evidence (packed_any_evidence_tp4_262144.json and ordered_writer_evidence_tp4.json at their pins), WITHOUT a baked default: the
# eight-seat 131k image tp4-serve-8 stays what ships until the owner says otherwise. Each job names its profile explicitly. A commit that changes a file the
# image carries needs a new SB9 build and a new tag in every template.
# H9: hand the cards back. The LAST card job of the window, and it runs even when a stop job halted the window and after a stall or a hang, which can leave all four cards hung:
# the status of every board and the all-four reset. It decides nothing about WHAT is placed; the driver does, in this order after H9: (1) the platform's fabric re-measure (it must
# pass before any placement, and A9 does not run without it); (2) the placement: TODAY'S PRODUCTION RECIPE (the image and profile that served before the window, c2-packed-tp4 with its
# cap of four, or the eight-seat 131k image tp4-serve-8 if the owner has shipped it); NEVER a gate arm, never a 262k profile by an environment variable; (3) the topology tick;
# (4) A9. A 262k placement exists only after the owner's decision on this window's evidence and a SEPARATE build that bakes it.
# Duration (estimate): 15 min. Stop rule: any failure stops the window (the placement steps are the driver's).
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=status reset
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-262k8-1
